    "body": "Also from the Hub review: the Tormach mill goldens open with `(VMC 3-AXIS)` and have no other comments. `tormach.cps` `onOpen` writes the machine file's `name` as the header comment. These goldens are posted against the generic `assets/machines/3axis-vmc.mch` (\"VMC 3-AXIS\"), not a Tormach machine. The bare CL fixtures also carry no SetupName, OperationName or tool parameters, so the post writes no `(SETUP: ...)`, `(OPERATION: ...)` or `(T.. ...)` lines. The lathe goldens do have them, e.g. `(TestBench PathPilot lathe)`, `(OPERATION: TH1 - THREADING - G54)` and `(T0101 TD-1732-60 - THREADING INSERT)`.\n\nAdd to *Done means*: post the Tormach mill goldens against a Tormach machine file (e.g. a 770MX), from a fixture with setup, operation and tool names. Then the header, op and tool comments appear the way they do in a real program.",
